-- CpuPool: caller timeout
ok   caller timeout -> PoolTimeout
ok   expired queued task is not started
ok   full queue -> PoolTimeout, task is not run
-- CpuPool: worker recovery
ok   both workers started
ok   SystemExit in task -> WorkerLost, worker replaced
ok   pool runs tasks after worker replacement
ok   kill during task: caller immediately gets WorkerLost
ok   after kill: two workers restored and busy is correct
ok   task finishing after deadline is counted in overran
ok   after close: new work rejected and workers exit without replacement
-- CpuPool: deterministic interruption (test holds pool mutex)
ok   kill after pop, before busy accounting: immediate WorkerLost
ok   busy unchanged and worker restored
ok   kill after task, before accounting: WorkerLost and busy returns to 0
ok   shutdown interrupts running task without replacement
ok   infinite timeout rejected
